mage": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/12"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/13"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/14"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/15"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/16"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/17"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017-01_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "[18]", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/18"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD6", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "editorialPageNumber": "2", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/21225849/21225849-0002.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\">umstances are calculated to awaken our spirits to a sacred rememberance of evry thing and we think that yours are also and that nothing therefore can seperate us from the love of God,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11835771048848654954\"><a href=\"#11835771048848654954\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans7\"><span id=\"documenttrans7\">7</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Romans 8:35, 39.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and fellowship one with another and that evry species of wickedness and cruelty practised upon us will only tend to bind our harts together and seal them together in love<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"521269437762655223\"><a href=\"#521269437762655223\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Colossians 2:2.</p><hr></div></div></aside> we have no need to say to you that we are held in bonds without cause neither is it needfull that you say unto us we are driven from our homes and smitten without cause. We mutually understand that if the inhabitance of the state of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14168678660069986006\"><a href=\"#14168678660069986006\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc140\" place=\"plc140\" title=\"Missouri\">Missouri</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Missouri\"><p>Area acquired by U.S. in Louisiana Purchase, 1803, and established as territory, 1812. Missouri Compromise, 1820, admitted Missouri as slave state, 1821. Population in 1830 about 140,000; in 1836 about 240,000; and in 1840 about 380,000. Latter-day Saint ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/missouri\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> had let the saints alone and had been as deserable of peace as they ware there would have been nothing but peace and quiatude [quietude] in this <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"3020826077919670316\"><a href=\"#3020826077919670316\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc140\" place=\"plc140\" title=\"Missouri\">State</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Missouri\"><p>Area acquired by U.S. in Louisiana Purchase, 1803, and established as territory, 1812. Missouri Compromise, 1820, admitted Missouri as slave state, 1821. Population in 1830 about 140,000; in 1836 about 240,000; and in 1840 about 380,000. Latter-day Saint ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/missouri\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> unto this day we should not have been in this hell surrounded with demonds if not those who are damned, they are those who shall be damned and where we are compeled to hear nothing but blasphemous oaths and witness a seen of blasphemy and drunkeness and hypocracy and debaucheries of evry description. And again the cries of orphans and widdows would not have assended up to God. the blood of inocent women and children yea and of men also would not have cried to God against them <span class=\"josephswriting\">it</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"2776314328077191410\"><a href=\"#2776314328077191410\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans2\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>would <span class=\"josephswriting\">not</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4220109228167618039\"><a href=\"#4220109228167618039\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans3\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>have stained the soyl of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"674501382885429723\"><a href=\"#674501382885429723\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc140\" place=\"plc140\" title=\"Missouri\">Missouri</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Missouri\"><p>Area acquired by U.S. in Louisiana Purchase, 1803, and established as territory, 1812. Missouri Compromise, 1820, admitted Missouri as slave state, 1821. Population in 1830 about 140,000; in 1836 about 240,000; and in 1840 about 380,000. Latter-day Saint ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/missouri\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9178644640341849757\"><a href=\"#9178644640341849757\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Genesis 4:10–11. For more information on <a href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Latter-day Saint</a> casualties during the 1838 conflict, see <a href=\"/intro/documents-volume-6-part-3-introduction-4-november-1838-16-april-1839\" class=\"article\">Introduction to Part 3: 4 Nov. 1838–16 Apr. 1839</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside> but oh! the unrelenting hand the inhumanity and murderous disposition of this people it shocks all nature it beggers and defies all discription. it is a tail [tale] of [p. 2]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\">umstances are calculated to awaken our spirits to a <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>sacred rememberance of evry thing and we think <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that yours are also and that nothing therefore can <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>seperate us from the love of God,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"9199737427887128619\"><a href=\"#9199737427887128619\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans7\"><span id=\"documenttrans7\">7</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Romans 8:35, 39.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and fellowship one <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>with another and that evry species of wickedness <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and cruelty practised upon us will only tend to <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>bind our harts together and seal them together in <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>love<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"18081406371185578673\"><a href=\"#18081406371185578673\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans8\"><span id=\"documenttrans8\">8</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Colossians 2:2.</p><hr></div></div></aside> we have no need to say to you that we are <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>held in bonds without cause neither is it needfull that <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>you say unto us we are driven from our homes <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and smitten without cause. We mutually unders[t]and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>that if the inhabitance of the state of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13278371344544194295\"><a href=\"#13278371344544194295\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc140\" place=\"plc140\" title=\"Missouri\">Missouri</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Missouri\"><p>Area acquired by U.S. in Louisiana Purchase, 1803, and established as territory, 1812. Missouri Compromise, 1820, admitted Missouri as slave state, 1821. Population in 1830 about 140,000; in 1836 about 240,000; and in 1840 about 380,000. Latter-day Saint ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/missouri\">More Info</a></div></div></aside> had let <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the saints alone and had been as deserable of peace <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>as they ware there would have been nothing but <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>peace and quiatude [quietude] in this &lt;​<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1099946692452745007\"><a href=\"#1099946692452745007\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc140\" place=\"plc140\" title=\"Missouri\">State</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Missouri\"><p>Area acquired by U.S. in Louisiana Purchase, 1803, and established as territory, 1812. Missouri Compromise, 1820, admitted Missouri as slave state, 1821. Population in 1830 about 140,000; in 1836 about 240,000; and in 1840 about 380,000. Latter-day Saint ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/missouri\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>​&gt; unto this day we should <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>not have been in this hell surrounded with demonds <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>if not those who are damned, they are those who shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>be damned and where we are compeled to hear nothing <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>but blasphemo[u]s oaths and witness a seen of blasphemy <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and drunkeness and hypocracy and debaucheries <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of evry description. And again the <span class=\"deleted\">cry</span> cries of orphans and <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>widdows would &lt;​not​&gt; have assended up to God. the blood <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>of inocent women and children yea and of men <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>also would not have cried to God against them <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>&lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">it</span>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10028883411927286094\"><a href=\"#10028883411927286094\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans2\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>would &lt;​<span class=\"josephswriting\">not</span>​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10784186167278422663\"><a href=\"#10784186167278422663\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans3\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of JS.</p><hr></div></div></aside><span class=\"josephswriting\"> </span>have stained the soyl of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12854898402208710361\"><a href=\"#12854898402208710361\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"plc140\" place=\"plc140\" title=\"Missouri\">Missouri</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Missouri\"><p>Area acquired by U.S. in Louisiana Purchase, 1803, and established as territory, 1812. Missouri Compromise, 1820, admitted Missouri as slave state, 1821. Population in 1830 about 140,000; in 1836 about 240,000; and in 1840 about 380,000. Latter-day Saint ...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/missouri\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17916063080573552285\"><a href=\"#17916063080573552285\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans9\"><span id=\"documenttrans9\">9</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Genesis 4:10–11. For more information on <a href=\"/topic/church-of-christ\" class=\"referenceInPop\">Latter-day Saint</a> casualties during the 1838 conflict, see <a href=\"/intro/documents-volume-6-part-3-introduction-4-november-1838-16-april-1839\" class=\"article\">Introduction to Part 3: 4 Nov. 1838–16 Apr. 1839</a>.</p><hr></div></div></aside> but oh! <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the unrelenting hand the inhumanity and murderous <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>disposition of this people it shocks all nature it <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>beggers and defies all discription. it is a tail [tale] of [p. 2]</div></body></html>", "calendarsOfDocuments": [], "versions": [{"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "versionLink": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/1", "versionFeatured": "true"}, {"versionTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839, as Published in <em xmlns:tei=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" xmlns:lds=\"https:/